{
  "outcome": "pending_approval",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Tom, thanks for reporting this. Your password isn't the cause. Your account got locked after several failed sign-in attempts this morning, and that's why the VPN keeps saying login failed. I've asked a technician to unlock it. Once they approve it, you should be able to connect to the VPN with your current password. Most of the failed attempts came from the office network around the time you also signed in successfully. That usually means a phone or second device still has an old password saved, for example the mail app on your phone. Please check your other devices and update or re-enter the password on any of them, or the account may lock again. If it still won't connect after the unlock, reply here and we'll keep looking.",
  "internal_note": "KB-013 checks: account status LOCKED (failed_login_count 5), sign_in_blocked false, vpn_access true. Duo is enrolled (duo_push on Tom's phone). Sign-in logs: 5 failed_password attempts on m365 on Fri 2026-10-09 between 09:20 and 09:35 ET. All came from corporate IP 203.0.113.10 in New York, inside his usual hours, with no hosting networks or foreign locations. A successful Duo sign-in at 09:28 sits in between the failures, which points to a second device with a stale saved password, not an attack. VPN history from his residential IP (198.51.100.24) has been consistently successful. Password last set 2026-07-23. Following KB-001, I queued unlock_account (approval id 1). I did not request a reset because the user says he knows his password. Escalate per KB-001 if it locks again within an hour after he updates his saved passwords.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-013",
    "KB-001"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
